   "subject": "DA  and asymetric components from bilat.symmetry",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi all, </div><div><br></div><div>I used the bilat.symmetry function my dataset (53 landmarks, 688 individual) and got the DA component, but it has the dimensions (53,2,2). What does this represent? I would have thought it would give me some sort of output showing the average deviation of each point from it&#39;s paired point, and the average deviation of the unpaired points from the median line, but that wouldn&#39;t account for the 3rd dimension?</div><div><br></div><div>Also, what exactly is the asymmetric component of variation? I&#39;ve read multiple sources but still don&#39;t understand - I get that the symmetric component is just a symmetrical version of the face, but what is the asymmetric component?</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>Richie</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hoqc8fSuAgAJ",
