   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] DA  and asymetric components from bilat.symmetry",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Dean,<div><br></div><div>for DA component the help file reads &quot;The directional asymmetry component, found as the mean shape for each side.&quot; I don&#39;t see how this corresponds to a 53 x 2 x 2 dataset. I get that the second and 3rd dimension are x,y and face side respectively, but each side of the face doesn&#39;t have 53 landmarks&gt;? </div><div><br></div><div>Sorry, I I think I asked a different question to the one I wanted an answer for. The asymmetric component of variation is well described in the literature, but what isn&#39;t clear to me is how it relates to the output of the bilat.symmetry function. The symmetric component seems to be the aligned coordinates after the face has been made symmetrical, but I don&#39;t understand what the coordinates given by the asymmetric component represent?</div><div><br></div><div>Richie</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Thursday, March 1, 2018 at 5:40:24 PM UTC, Dean Adams wrote:</div></div>"
